#!/bin/bash
set -euo pipefail
python3 -c 'import sys,json,collections
k="control_id|title|cis_section|severity|asset_scope|threat_mapping|implementation_task|verification_method|justification".split("|")
c=list(map(lambda s:dict(zip(k,s.rstrip("\n").split("|"))),sys.stdin)); n=collections.Counter(map(lambda x:x["severity"],c)); sections=set(map(lambda x:x["cis_section"],c)); tasks=set(map(lambda x:x["implementation_task"],c))
assert len(c)==15 and n=={"critical":5,"high":7,"medium":3} and len(sections)==5 and len(tasks)==10 and all(map(lambda x:set(x)==set(k),c))
open("cis_profile.json","w").write(json.dumps({"profile":"MedDefense Linux threat-driven CIS control profile","benchmark_reference":"Ubuntu 22.04 CIS-inspired thematic mapping; verify exact control numbering against chosen benchmark edition","controls":c},indent=2)+"\n")
print("Controls selected: 15\nCritical: 5\nHigh: 7\nMedium: 3\nCIS sections covered: 5\nMapped implementation tasks: 10\nReport saved to: cis_profile.json")
' <<'DATA'
MD-CIS-01|Disable direct SSH root login|4 Access Authentication and Authorization|critical|billing-srv-01,web-srv-01,log-srv-01|SSH lateral movement,privilege escalation|SSH_HARDEN|sshd -T confirms permitrootlogin no|Direct root access removes account attribution and enables privileged lateral movement
MD-CIS-02|Require key-based SSH after access validation|4 Access Authentication and Authorization|critical|billing-srv-01,web-srv-01,log-srv-01|weak authentication,SSH lateral movement|SSH_HARDEN|Verified key login succeeds and sshd -T shows passwordauthentication no|Passwords are reusable or guessable; lockout prevention requires testing keys first
MD-CIS-03|Enforce PAM password quality and lockout|4 Access Authentication and Authorization|critical|billing-srv-01,web-srv-01,log-srv-01|weak authentication,credential stuffing|PAM_POLICY|Inspect pam-auth-update profiles and test pam_pwquality and pam_faillock where supported|Weak passwords and unrestricted guesses expose administrative access
MD-CIS-04|Restrict database listening and access|3 Network Configuration|critical|billing-srv-01|exposed database services,data theft|DB_EXPOSURE|ss -lntup and database bind plus firewall ACL review|Billing data is at risk when database sockets accept broad network connections
MD-CIS-05|Enable security audit events and forwarding|5 Logging and Auditing|critical|billing-srv-01,web-srv-01,log-srv-01|missing audit visibility,incident response gaps|AUDIT_ENABLE|systemctl is-active auditd and auditctl -l plus remote receipt test|Reliable security events are necessary to reconstruct lateral movement
MD-CIS-06|Minimize SSH authentication attempts and forwarding|4 Access Authentication and Authorization|high|billing-srv-01,web-srv-01,log-srv-01|SSH lateral movement,brute force|SSH_HARDEN|sshd -T checks maxauthtries and x11forwarding|Limit guessing opportunities and unnecessary SSH channels
MD-CIS-07|Disable unused network-facing services|2 Services|high|billing-srv-01,web-srv-01,log-srv-01|unnecessary services,remote exploitation|SERVICE_MIN|Compare systemctl enabled units and ss listeners against approved service inventory|Reducing exposed daemons lowers reachable attack surface
MD-CIS-08|Harden IPv4 redirects and source routing|3 Network Configuration|high|billing-srv-01,web-srv-01,log-srv-01|kernel hardening gaps,traffic interception|SYSCTL_HARDEN|sysctl -a checks accept_redirects and accept_source_route across interfaces|Reject spoofed route controls that can facilitate interception
MD-CIS-09|Enable kernel exploit mitigations|3 Network Configuration|high|billing-srv-01,web-srv-01,log-srv-01|kernel hardening gaps,privilege escalation|SYSCTL_HARDEN|sysctl checks kernel.randomize_va_space and kernel.dmesg_restrict|Kernel safeguards reduce useful information leaks and exploit reliability
MD-CIS-10|Enforce host firewall least privilege|3 Network Configuration|high|billing-srv-01,web-srv-01,log-srv-01|exposed database services,lateral movement|FIREWALL_POLICY|nft list ruleset or ufw status and test permitted source-to-port reachability|Allow only approved management and application flows per server role
MD-CIS-11|Protect account and credential files|1 Initial Setup|high|billing-srv-01,web-srv-01,log-srv-01|weak authentication,credential disclosure|FILE_PERMS|stat -c %a:%U:%G for /etc/shadow /etc/passwd and SSH files|Loose credential-file permissions expose account data to local users
MD-CIS-12|Audit privilege changes and authentication|5 Logging and Auditing|high|billing-srv-01,web-srv-01,log-srv-01|missing audit visibility,privilege abuse|AUDIT_ENABLE|auditctl -l or augenrules --check and controlled sudo event search|Track sensitive privilege and identity changes for forensic attribution
MD-CIS-13|Eliminate unapproved world-writable files|1 Initial Setup|medium|billing-srv-01,web-srv-01,log-srv-01|filesystem permission misuse,local persistence|FILE_PERMS|find approved local filesystems -xdev -type f -perm -0002 and review exceptions|Writable files may allow tampering or persistence in unsafe locations
MD-CIS-14|Set persistent log retention and rotation|5 Logging and Auditing|medium|billing-srv-01,web-srv-01,log-srv-01|insufficient log retention,incident evidence loss|LOG_RETENTION|Inspect journald Storage and SystemMaxUse plus logrotate policy and retention test|Logs must survive reboot and remain available for investigations
MD-CIS-15|Disable unneeded filesystem modules|1 Initial Setup|medium|billing-srv-01,web-srv-01,log-srv-01|unnecessary attack surface,kernel hardening gaps|MODULE_HARDEN|modprobe -n -v for selected unused modules and lsmod inspection|Blocking unused filesystem handlers removes unnecessary kernel attack paths
DATA
